    "notes": "One part (Soprano) with one lyric line, 39 bars on two pages.  Stanza 1 in Ab major, stanza 2 (bar 21, first bar of page 2) in E major: 4 cancelling naturals + 4 sharps, with the courtesy key signature at the end of page 1.  Spellings to preserve: C#5/D5 natural (bar 5), Cb5 (bar 8), Fb4 (bar 9), D natural then Db (bar 11), Gb5 and E natural (bars 14-15), Bbb4 (bar 18); in E major B#4 (bar 23, sounds C5 but octave 4), E#5 and F##5 (bar 24, melisma into G#5), D/C naturals and A#4 (bars 26-28), B#4 tied over the barline into bar 31, G naturals (bars 33-34), D natural then D# (bar 37).  The scans show the two pages side by side (2-up) or as separate pages at slightly different scales; the conversion must treat them as one continuous part."
  },
